GenCauseEvent: PROCEDURE(pMachine, event, param) CLEAN;
DCL pMachine			SELECTOR;
DCL event				BYTE;
DCL param				WORD;     

/*-------------------------------------------------------------------------

 purpose:   This procdeure allows the actions to generate another
      event to be processed after the action processing is
      done.

 inputs:  pMachine - Selector to the state machine control block.
      event - the event number to be caused.
      param - a word parameter to be passed to the action
        which is activated by the caused event.

 sideEffects: The caused event and param are stored in the state machine
      control block. 

 algorithm: 
  1) If a caused event has already been set up then call machine
   failure (should never have more than one caused event outstanding)
  2) Else put the caused event and parameter into the machine control
   block.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

DCL machine				BASED pMachine generalMachineType;

	IF machine.causedEvent = noCausedEvent THEN
	DO;
		machine.causedEvent = event;
		machine.causedParam = param;
	END;
	ELSE
		CALL GenMachineFailure(pMachine, null, tooManyCausedEvents);

END GenCauseEvent;

